; =====================================================================
; impactatc_m6_after_change.ngc - YOUR hook, run after every tool change
; Controller: LinuxCNC          Part of the ImpactATC M6 integration
;
; Called at the end of every successful M6 that leaves a tool in the
; spindle, with LinuxCNC's current tool already set to the new tool
; (#<_current_tool>) and the spindle stopped at safe Z.
;
; Empty by default. This is the place for tool-length measurement on a
; tool setter. Re-measuring after each ATC load is recommended: the
; seated depth of the collet can vary slightly between clamps.
;
; If you add a measurement, write the result into the tool table
; (G10 L1 P#<_current_tool> Z...) and leave G43 to your CAM program,
; which normally issues G43 H.. straight after M6.
; =====================================================================

o<impactatc_m6_after_change> sub

; ---- add your tool-length measurement here ----

o<impactatc_m6_after_change> endsub
